---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About & Editorial Standards"
  description="Who we are, how we research, and the standards every Naturally Restful article must meet."
>
  <div class="container">
    <h1 class="page-title">About Naturally Restful</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      We publish honest, research-aware guides about sleep and stress supplements — for readers
      in the US, UK, Canada, and Australia who are tired of hype.
    </p>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Why this site exists</h2>
      <p>
        Search for any sleep supplement and you'll find the same thing: pages written to sell,
        not to inform — miracle wording, fake urgency, and zero mention of what the research
        actually shows. Naturally Restful is the counterweight: we tell you what supplements
        can plausibly do, what they can't, and when you should skip them entirely.
      </p>

      <h2>Our editorial standards</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Human trials over hype.</strong> Claims are grounded in published human research, not marketing copy.</li>
        <li><strong>No disease claims.</strong> Supplements support sleep and relaxation; they do not diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent disease. We hold this line without exception.</li>
        <li><strong>Advertising never influences rankings.</strong> Commissions are the same regardless of which product you pick, so we pick on merit.</li>
        <li><strong>We name the weaknesses.</strong> Every supplement page includes who shouldn't take it and what the evidence doesn't show.</li>
        <li><strong>Corrections are public.</strong> When research updates, articles get an "Updated" date and the change is noted.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How we make money</h2>
      <p>
        Transparently: affiliate commissions. If you buy through a link on this site, the seller
        pays us a small commission at no extra cost to you. That's it — we don't sell your data,
        and we don't take money to rank a product. Read the full
        <a href="/disclosure">affiliate disclosure</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>A note on credentials — the honest version</h2>
      <p>
        We are researchers, not physicians, and we say so plainly (see
        <a href="/author">the author page</a>). Our job is to read and translate the science
        accurately; your doctor's job is to apply it to you. Both roles matter, and confusing
        them is how bad health content happens.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
